Episode 4 
The White Wolf

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.900
That should do it.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.820
Haro, switch to PC mode.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.610
Roger! Roger!

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.370
What are you doing, Flit?

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:08.290
I'm transferring all the data from the previous battles to the AGE system.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.250
Are you ready, Vargas?

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.420
Yup! Ready whenever!

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.340
I didn't know you could do that.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.680
This is an important duty, too.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.850
Duty... You're starting to sound like a soldier.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.600
Battles, huh?

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.270
Nora's gone, isn't it?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.060
What's going to happen to us next?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.440
What are Mom and Dad up to right now?

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:42.700
If you're worried,

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.870
then let's go ask the captain!

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.550
Mr. Grodek.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:05.600
There's something we wanted to ask you.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.390
Ask the rest of the crew.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.310
What's his problem?

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.770
He's creepy.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.770
I see, but that's not surprising.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.110
The captain is a busy man.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:20.650
What's going to happen to us now?

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:24.410
Right now, the ship is heading to Fardain for resupply.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.070
We'll arrive in seven days.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:31.120
I heard that the Nora citizens the Federation rescued were taken to Tordia.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.000
You can catch a ship to Tordia once we get to Fardain.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.670
The military will take care of your ticket.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.540
I'll try to contact your parents too.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:39.630
Really?

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.380
Yeah.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.800
Isn't that great, Dique?

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:43.590
Yeah!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.180
You sound like you're not included.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.970
You're coming too, right, Flit?{go vs come. i'm assuming what's her face is going to tordia too}

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.850
What is this?

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.140
Just <i>what </i> is going on here?{suggest italic "what", and change to "what is"}

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.770
Why aren't we at Nora?

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.440
When did we leave?

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.610
Was there really a battle?

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.530
And who are you guys, anyway?

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.780
It's Woolf Enneacle!

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.410
You know him?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.080
He's famous!

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.410
He used to be a star in the Mobile Suit Grand Prix race!

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.870
I heard he joined the Federation Forces. I guess he ended up on this ship!

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.380
I apologize for not introducing myself.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.960
I'm responsible for the ship's navigational control...

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.300
I'm not interested in hearing men introduce themselves. {lol}

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.090
I'd like to hear all about <i>you</i>, though.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.760
I refuse.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.180
She's Ms. Millais.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.350
I see. I'll call her Millie then.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.020
I refuse!

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.730
So anyway, what are these kids doing aboard a warship?

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.820
Since when was this a daycare center?

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:43.780
Daycare center?

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:47.110
They're children we rescued at Nora.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:49.530
We were suddenly attacked by the UE.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:53.370
Oh, so we panicked and ran.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:54.660
I see.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.660
But they're no ordinary kids.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:02.090
Flit here is the first human to defeat the UE.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.010
With a mobile suit he made himself.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.170
What?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.300
That joke's not funny.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.300
It's true!

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.470
Everything's been crazy since I woke up from healing sleep.{lol this music}

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.980
What's going on?

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:21.400
We were ordered to board this ship at Nora.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.520
Captain Grodek can tell you the details—

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.400
Grodek?

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.150
Who's that? When did we get a new captain?

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.160
No, never mind, don't answer that.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:33.030
I'll get the answers from this Grodek guy himself.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.290
What's with that guy?

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.500
He's Woolf Enneacle, I'm telling you!

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.920
A former star in the Grand Prix race!

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:48.010
He's a weird guy. Once there was nobody left for him to beat, he announced he was joining the military.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:51.800
With his animalistic intuition and unparalleled piloting skills,

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.350
he earned the nickname "The White Wolf" and became an ace pilot of the Federation Force.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.770
Is he really that great?

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.370
Hey, is everyone working hard?

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.750
All you mechanics!

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:19.910
He's back...

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:24.710
So this is my new mobile suit?

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.340
I like it.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.300
No. This is <i>my </i> mobile suit.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:31.680
It's called the Gundam.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.760
Oh, I see. Then I'll take it from you.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.220
Why?!

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:42.140
Do you know what they call me?

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.560
The White Wolf?

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:44.480
That's right.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.820
So I get the white mobile suit.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:51.240
In other words, this Gundam thing is my machine!

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:54.320
I'm asking you why!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:59.250
Because I'm the commander of this ship's mobile suit forces.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.370
Commander?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.670
Who said <i>that</i>?

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.130
Captain Grodek.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:09.670
The Captain just appointed me to this position himself.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.590
Of course, it was only natural considering my abilities.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.760
Not a good choice...

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:20.770
So the Gundam is mine. Understand?

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.020
No, I don't.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:22.770
You're not satisfied?

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:23.940
Of course not!

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.810
Then let's compete for it.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:27.020
Compete?

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.690
That's right.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:33.490
You and I will get in our mobile suits and have a one-on-one mock battle.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:36.570
If I win, the Gundam is mine.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:40.490
And if by some bizarre{small} chance I lose, I'll give up on it.

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:41.370
Well?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:43.250
The Gundam's not a toy!

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.920
I know. It's a weapon.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:49.340
Flit's talking back to him as if he were a soldier.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:53.720
What'll it be? If you like, you can just accept defeat right now.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.930
Fine! We'll take you on!

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:59.430
Emily! Why are you...?

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:05.020
If he loses the Gundam, he might stop acting like a soldier!

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.150
The girl seems to have more guts than you do.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:11.480
So what'll it be, kid?

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.860
Okay, I accept!

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.280
Then it's settled.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.870
<i>Deploying mobile suit catapults. {speaker}</i>

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:23.790
<i>The Gundam will launch first, followed by the Genoace Custom. {speaker}</i>

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:27.170
Is this really a good idea, Captain?

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.500
It'll be good training.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.510
Let's go, Gundam!

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:43.020
<i>The Gundam will launch from portside Chute 2. {speaker}</i>

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.890
<i>MS catapult station, begin entry sequence. {speaker}</i>

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:48.940
<i>Link between Gundam and launch control system confirmed. {speaker}</i>

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:51.770
<i>Activate synchrotron scan, accelerators 1 through 4. {speaker}</i>

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.610
<i>Gauging complete. All values normal. {speaker}</i>

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.700
<i>Moving to rotary action sequence. {speaker}</i>

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.240
<i>Catapult personnel, withdraw to the Operation Command Center. {speaker}</i>

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.700
<i>Pressure control system online. No change to internal pressure. {speaker}</i>

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:06.410
<i>Moving to launch sequence. Final confirmation of catapult launch path. {speaker}</i>

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:09.880
<i>No meteorite debris found in launch path. {speaker}</i>

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.460
<i>No problems with Chute 2 catapult launch. {speaker}</i>

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.130
<i>Launch preparations complete! {speaker}</i>

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:17.720
Flit Asuno, Gundam, here I go!

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.980
He can talk the talk, at least.{Oh, he's at least got spirit. But we might keep the metaphor here even if its not exactly right}

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:33.440
<i>Genoace Custom will now prepare for launch.</i>

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:34.730
Roger, roger.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:37.650
<i>Friendly unit "Gundam" inside patrol area. {speaker}</i>

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:39.360
<i>Maintain relative distance. {speaker}</i>

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.570
<i>Chute 1, launch preparations complete! {speaker}</i>

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:44.290
Woolf, Genoace Custom, heading out!

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:53.040
Don't forget the deal!

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.920
I won't lose!

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.810
This'll be a mock battle using these marker shots.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.730
They won't do any real damage if they hit,

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:17.990
but the computer will determine the damage they do.

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:19.650
The time limit is 30 minutes.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:24.580
<i>The one who gets the most hits and the most points by then, wins.</i>

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.490
Any questions?

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:28.000
None.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.960
Okay then, let's begin!

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.670
Who's going to win?

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.300
Normally, I'd say Woolf.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.470
Yeah. {i know right}{ikr}

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.550
But it's possible...

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.560
Are you ready?

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.230
Any time.

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:54.770
Ready.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:55.480
Go!

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.520
It's started!

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:58.570
Go, Woolf!

00:11:58.570 --> 00:11:59.530
Don't lose, Flit!

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.070
What's wrong?

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.370
Your aim's off!

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.670
What was that?

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:18.920
I forgot to mention, but being hit will result in a momentary electric shock.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.670
It's a punishment for sucking, you could say.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:23.340
Talking down to me...!

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:24.090
Take this!

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.270
I can't hit him! Why?

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:39.020
Flit!

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:42.860
He's gonna lose before he even gets a hit in!

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.780
What are you doing, Flit?

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.120
You need to watch his movements!

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.740
Watch his movements?

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:54.040
That's right! I did it with the UE, didn't I?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.680
You can't win a fight just by watching!

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.160
What?

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.490
He did it! He got him!

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.910
Great job, Flit! Get him!

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.170
What?

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:37.370
Nothing.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.080
He's not bad.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.130
Yes, Flit's amazing!

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:48.510
So it looks like you weren't <i>all </i> talk.{at least}

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.770
The Gundam is my mobile suit!

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:58.600
It's time for me to get serious!

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:01.690
Sounds good to me!

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.080
An enemy!

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.450
So this is the UE?

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:24.420
The Gundam and the Genoace Custom have made contact with an enemy believed to be the UE!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.960
They're in a combat situation!

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.380
All hands to level 1 battle stations! Hurry!

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.100
<i>All hands to level 1 battle stations!</i>

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:33.060
<i>Level 1 battle stations!</i>

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.430
What are you doing, Emily?

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:38.480
No way... Flit...

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.070
Damn! We can't beat them with marker shots...

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:52.280
Vargas, launch the DODS rifle!

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.450
I know! I'm getting it ready!

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.240
It's coming!

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:00.830
You get back!

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:02.040
No, you get back, Mr. Woolf!

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:02.880
What?

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:05.800
I've fought the UE before!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.550
The Gundam can beat them!

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:09.260
Hey!

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:22.400
I can do it! It'll be just like Nora...

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:24.230
I'll use the beam dagger!

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:27.190
He's...

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:35.120
What are you doing?

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:36.030
Shut up!

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:42.080
I was just about to beat it!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.540
Just be quiet!

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:44.380
Don't move!

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.710
Look over there.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:09.230
Flit, come in!

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:10.690
Flit, Woolf!

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:13.030
What's wrong? Give me a report.

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:18.330
The Gundam and Genoace Custom have vanished, along with the enemy mobile suit-type!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.080
Vanished?!

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:22.000
Captain, let's go after them!

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:24.330
The Diva will remain on standby.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.420
Captain!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:29.090
We can't send this ship in until we know what's going on.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:31.550
Prioritize surveillance of the surrounding area.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:36.850
Grandpa, what's going on?

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:39.430
I heard they disappeared from the scanners...

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:41.430
Calm down, Emily.

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:43.770
For now we need to believe in Flit and wait.{is this the second time he said to believe in flit and just wait?}

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.610
What do we do now?

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:55.070
With our current equipment we can't even put up a fight.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:58.030
Thankfully, they don't seem to have noticed us.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:00.410
We stay quiet and let them pass.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:05.460
I don't know how they're doing it, but even this close, I can't detect that huge ship.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.420
We'll just have to wait.

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:21.970
Mr. Woolf...

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:27.810
I know. So don't move.

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:39.530
Hey!

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.670
You idiot!

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:50.840
Mr. Woolf!

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:56.130
You get back to the Diva! You know roughly where it is, right?

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:56.760
But...

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.430
I'm not doing this for you! {i'm not doing this for you/your sake!}

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.430
Let them all know about the enemy ship!

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:04.220
Go!

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:13.360
I'll show you what The White Wolf can do!

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.400
I'm getting something on the search system!

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.780
A friendly signal?

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:18.530
It's the Gundam!

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:21.330
Open a channel!

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:24.040
Flit, can you hear me? Come in!

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:25.580
Ms. Millais!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:26.290
Flit!

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:28.040
Send out the DODS rifle!

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.000
What are you doing? Hurry!

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:32.880
Vargas, you're ready, right?

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:34.090
I'm ready whenever!

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:36.840
All right! Launch the DODS rifle!

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:50.400
Flit!

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:54.320
Everyone stay back! There are enemies here! Tons of them!

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:55.570
Enemies?

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:57.400
Tons of them?

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:59.780
Set a course for the direction the Gundam came from.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.780
Maybe I overdid the cool-guy act.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:48.370
That's...

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:50.910
The Gundam!

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:58.340
Why did you come back?

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:01.220
I told the Diva what's going on!{hardly}

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:04.090
But there are so many...

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:14.270
That's it!

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:15.270
Give me that.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:16.440
What?

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:16.080
They're gone?

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:19.960
I don't get it, but we're saved.

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:23.380
Thank you, Mr. Woolf.

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:26.800
You didn't do too badly either.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:35.940
Jeez, you guys went all out.

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:37.810
Show some consideration for the guys that have to fix it.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.190
Don't complain.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.900
I hear things were pretty close this time.

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:43.940
The pilots are always risking their lives out there.

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:48.700
I was fine!

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:52.200
Sure you were. You were about to cry!

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:57.000
And then I told you, "A man should never give up! There's still a chance!"

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.670
You never said anything like that!

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:01.540
I was the one who came back for you after I told the Diva!

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:01.840
Yeah.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.550
I came back to save you!

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:04.550
Are you even listening to me, Mr. Woolf?

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:04.550
Yeah.

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:17.600
It looks like the enemy has some way of avoiding detection by radar and optical sensors.

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:19.850
An invisible umbrella...

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:25.320
I've figured out what the UE really are...

